      HOWPERMS
PERMS N IS A MATRIX OF !N ROWS AND N COLUMNS, EVERY ORDER OF
1 TO N ONCE. IT IS BUILT UP FROM PERMS 1: EACH NEW NUMBER K
IS PUT INTO EVERY PERMUTATION OF 1 TO K-1 AT EVERY ONE OF
ITS K POSITIONS. THE ROWS COME OUT GROUPED BY THAT POSITION,
NOT IN DICTIONARY ORDER; PERMS 5 HAS 120 ROWS, PERMS 7 5040,
AND THE WORKSPACE WILL NOT HOLD MANY MORE.
      HOWBASE
B BASE N IS THE DIGITS OF N IN BASE B, MOST SIGNIFICANT
FIRST, AS MANY AS N NEEDS; B UNBASE D TURNS THEM BACK. THEY
ARE ENCODE AND DECODE, ⊤ AND ⊥, WITH THE NUMBER OF DIGITS
WORKED OUT FOR YOU. DIGITS N IS 10 BASE N.

